<title>SPAIN: PESETA DEBT/INTERBANK CLOSING REPORT.</title>
<headline>PESETA DEBT/INTERBANK CLOSING REPORT.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish government bonds closed largely unchanged on Friday after an active session in which the short-end sparkled and the long-end languished, dealers said.</p>
<p>Curve trades focused much of the session's activity, with selling at the long end and buying at the short end.</p>
<p>&quot;There appears to be a lot more confidence in the short end,&quot; said one dealer. &quot;This is backed up by the difference in spreads between the short and long end.&quot;</p>
<p>Dealers said the trend in Bunds continued to provide direction for bonos. Spanish bonds drew strength in late trade from a fall in the dollar, they added.</p>
</text>
